  "body": "What happens: the test `slot_dxf_sketch::a_slot_outline_seeds_the_slot_and_cuts_it_to_size` fails on `upstream/main` at `dfbe0d8a5`.\n\n```\ngolden crates/app/tests/golden/slot_dxf_outline.cl is stale; regenerate with WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test\n```\n\nThe committed golden is `HSMW-CL v1` with 9 moves. The generator now writes `HSMW-CL v2` with 15 moves. The new moves go back along the slot and add four arcs at the slot ends (`Arc ... I45000 J25000`, `Arc ... I75000 J25000`).\n\nExpected: the test passes on `main`.\n\nEvidence:\n- Command: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test slot_dxf_sketch a_slot_outline_seeds_the_slot_and_cuts_it_to_size`.\n- It fails on unchanged `upstream/main` (`dfbe0d8a5`) in a clean worktree.\n- It fails in the same way on the #1914 branch, which does not change toolpath code.\n- The last commits that touch the test or the golden: `dde391f76` and `bd24b9328`.\n\nFound while gating #1914.\n\nOpen question: is the new path (a second pass with arcs at the slot ends) correct, or is it a regression? Read the generator change before you regenerate the golden.\n\nDone means: the golden agrees with a path that is shown correct, and the test is green on `main`.\n",
